00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:06,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,745 --> 00:01:38,905
ADAPTED FROM THE EARLY SPRING ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:49,625 --> 00:01:50,505
Is that him?

4
00:01:51,785 --> 00:01:52,625
That's him.

5
00:01:53,585 --> 00:01:54,745
I've seen his picture.

6
00:01:54,825 --> 00:01:56,985
He sure looks decent. That's him.

7
00:01:57,065 --> 00:01:58,505
Anyone who bullies our daughter
is no better than a dog.

8
00:01:58,585 --> 00:02:00,345
-I'm going to have a word with him.
-No, come back!

9
00:02:01,225 --> 00:02:02,385
-Come back.
-What's wrong?

10
00:02:02,465 --> 00:02:04,105
What are you doing?

11
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:05,745
Tao isn't back yet.

12
00:02:05,825 --> 00:02:06,945
You're not young anymore.

13
00:02:07,025 --> 00:02:09,584
Trying to pick a fight with him? Honestly.

14
00:02:09,665 --> 00:02:10,945
Doesn't he get under your skin?

15
00:02:11,505 --> 00:02:12,985
Keep it down.

16
00:02:13,065 --> 00:02:14,225
Why should we serve him?

17
00:02:14,305 --> 00:02:16,385
Why feed him? You're treating him
like our son-in-law now.

18
00:02:16,465 --> 00:02:18,505
I didn't serve him.

19
00:02:18,585 --> 00:02:20,545
I didn't even bring out
the dishes he ordered.

20
00:02:20,625 --> 00:02:25,225
He helped himself to the peanuts
and the drinks.

21
00:02:25,305 --> 00:02:26,785
Was I supposed to stop him from drinking?

22
00:02:26,865 --> 00:02:27,945
Jeez.

23
00:02:28,025 --> 00:02:29,185
Boss, bill, please.

24
00:02:29,265 --> 00:02:30,385
Coming.

25
00:02:31,545 --> 00:02:33,545
Here you go. That'll be 150.

26
00:02:37,305 --> 00:02:40,105
Tao, where are you?

27
00:02:40,185 --> 00:02:41,105
Hurry home.

28
00:02:41,185 --> 00:02:42,545
Thank you.

29
00:02:42,625 --> 00:02:43,825
Alright. See you.

30
00:02:57,865 --> 00:02:59,345
We're closed.

31
00:03:03,025 --> 00:03:03,865
Mr. Shang,

32
00:03:04,465 --> 00:03:06,785
it's only eight.
The sign says you close at ten.

33
00:03:07,465 --> 00:03:08,945
Don't call me that.

34
00:03:09,025 --> 00:03:10,825
I own this place.

35
00:03:10,905 --> 00:03:12,825
I'll close whenever I want.

36
00:03:13,465 --> 00:03:15,265
Mr. Shang, I'm waiting for someone.

37
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:17,425
I told you not to call me that.

38
00:03:18,225 --> 00:03:21,385
Listen. Stop wasting your time.

39
00:03:21,465 --> 00:03:23,425
The person you're waiting for
is not coming today.

40
00:03:24,025 --> 00:03:26,545
How about this?
You and Mrs. Shang go upstairs first.

41
00:03:26,625 --> 00:03:27,585
I'll mind the shop.

42
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:29,305
I'm not leaving until Tao comes back.

43
00:03:29,865 --> 00:03:31,225
Who says you can call her "Tao"?

44
00:03:38,025 --> 00:03:41,465
LUKE IS MY DOG TOO

45
00:03:43,705 --> 00:03:45,745
Who says you can call her "Tao"?

46
00:03:54,865 --> 00:03:55,705
You're back.

47
00:03:57,265 --> 00:03:58,105
Dad,

48
00:03:58,625 --> 00:04:00,385
I'll close up tonight.
You two go upstairs.

49
00:04:01,585 --> 00:04:02,625
Don't worry.

50
00:04:11,225 --> 00:04:13,865
In that case, take care of yourself.

51
00:04:46,745 --> 00:04:47,665
Mr. Luan,

52
00:04:48,265 --> 00:04:49,705
our tavern is tiny.

53
00:04:50,585 --> 00:04:51,825
Why don't you grab a drink somewhere else?

54
00:04:53,185 --> 00:04:54,345
Let's talk somewhere else.

55
00:04:54,425 --> 00:04:55,625
No need.

56
00:04:58,665 --> 00:05:00,865
If you want to discuss work,
come to the office.

57
00:05:00,945 --> 00:05:04,105
There's nothing to talk about here.

58
00:05:08,265 --> 00:05:09,305
You've always held a grudge against me.

59
00:05:14,265 --> 00:05:18,945
How could I? You're such a big shot.

60
00:05:20,025 --> 00:05:21,465
Why would I hold a grudge?

61
00:05:28,145 --> 00:05:28,985
Tao.

62
00:05:30,265 --> 00:05:31,905
Can you please talk to me nicely?

63
00:05:33,025 --> 00:05:34,865
It's not that I can't.

64
00:05:37,345 --> 00:05:39,545
I just don't have anything to say to you.

65
00:06:09,225 --> 00:06:12,185
You've received 10,000 yuan via Alipay.

66
00:06:16,585 --> 00:06:17,465
Luan Nian.

67
00:06:20,305 --> 00:06:21,705
It's only one plate of peanuts
and one bottle of soda.

68
00:06:21,785 --> 00:06:22,705
Why did you pay 10,000?

69
00:06:22,785 --> 00:06:25,385
If you're that rich,
why don't you just buy this tavern?

70
00:06:27,345 --> 00:06:28,305
Would you sell it?

71
00:06:30,385 --> 00:06:32,305
Everything has a price in your eyes.

72
00:06:33,345 --> 00:06:35,465
Why did you sell
the bags and gifts I gave you?

73
00:06:39,585 --> 00:06:44,465
If it's because I sold your gifts
and left without saying goodbye,

74
00:06:44,545 --> 00:06:45,785
I'll apologize.

75
00:06:47,145 --> 00:06:49,025
I haven't spent a single cent
from selling those bags.

76
00:06:49,105 --> 00:06:50,825
If you want it back,
give me your account number.

77
00:06:51,985 --> 00:06:53,185
I'll transfer the money back.

78
00:06:53,265 --> 00:06:54,305
If you don't,

79
00:06:54,385 --> 00:06:57,305
I'll donate it when I get the chance.
How does that sound?

80
00:07:00,985 --> 00:07:01,825
Keep it.

81
00:07:06,745 --> 00:07:07,585
Alright.

82
00:07:09,305 --> 00:07:10,265
I'll keep it.

83
00:07:12,145 --> 00:07:13,225
Now we're even.

84
00:07:16,385 --> 00:07:17,585
Shang Zhitao.

85
00:07:22,105 --> 00:07:23,065
I'll come back tomorrow.

86
00:07:23,865 --> 00:07:25,505
What exactly do you want?

87
00:07:27,545 --> 00:07:30,145
You want to tell my parents about
what happened between us, don't you?

88
00:07:30,745 --> 00:07:31,905
You don't have to.

89
00:07:31,985 --> 00:07:33,705
I'll tell them right now.

90
00:07:33,785 --> 00:07:36,225
I behaved badly.

91
00:07:36,305 --> 00:07:38,345
I got involved with you
because I wanted to climb the ladder.

92
00:07:43,465 --> 00:07:45,425
I've never thought
of our relationship that way.

93
00:07:46,465 --> 00:07:47,345
Shang Zhitao,

94
00:07:48,905 --> 00:07:50,705
I truly loved you during those six years.

95
00:07:55,065 --> 00:07:55,985
That doesn't matter anymore.

96
00:07:59,025 --> 00:08:00,385
We're over.

97
00:08:12,105 --> 00:08:12,945
Luan Nian,

98
00:08:14,985 --> 00:08:16,265
I'm really tired.

99
00:08:20,305 --> 00:08:22,785
I've barely slept for two days
because of this summit.

100
00:08:26,505 --> 00:08:27,825
Can I drive you home?

101
00:08:28,905 --> 00:08:31,385
When you're exhausted,
driving is dangerous.

102
00:08:39,545 --> 00:08:40,865
OLD COUPLE'S TAVERN

103
00:08:55,905 --> 00:08:57,305
Follow the GPS.

104
00:09:13,785 --> 00:09:15,705
Today's high in Harbin
is minus 13 degrees.

105
00:09:15,785 --> 00:09:18,145
The low is minus 22 degrees.

106
00:09:18,225 --> 00:09:20,025
It's bitterly cold and humid.

107
00:09:20,105 --> 00:09:22,705
Bundle up to keep from getting sick.

108
00:11:08,505 --> 00:11:09,505
Hello?

109
00:11:11,145 --> 00:11:12,105
I'm home.

110
00:11:13,145 --> 00:11:14,625
I'll come get it from you tomorrow.

111
00:11:15,665 --> 00:11:16,785
No need to pick me up.

112
00:11:16,865 --> 00:11:17,705
Okay.

113
00:11:18,945 --> 00:11:19,825
See you tomorrow.

114
00:11:45,225 --> 00:11:46,465
How are you getting back?

115
00:11:48,305 --> 00:11:50,505
It's okay. I can get back by myself.

116
00:11:52,665 --> 00:11:53,505
Thanks.

117
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:07,665
LUMI

118
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:10,305
Mr. Luan seems to have taken quite a blow.

119
00:13:10,385 --> 00:13:12,105
He suddenly disappeared.

120
00:13:12,825 --> 00:13:14,505
Are you two together?

121
00:14:20,785 --> 00:14:23,585
Luan Nian, have you lost your mind?
What are you doing out here?

122
00:14:26,665 --> 00:14:27,705
It's freezing.

123
00:14:29,225 --> 00:14:31,745
I thought I'd have a drink to warm up.

124
00:14:33,105 --> 00:14:34,665
Are you trying to freeze to death?

125
00:14:34,745 --> 00:14:36,265
Do you think I'd take responsibility
if something happened to you?

126
00:14:38,705 --> 00:14:40,705
-Would you?
-No.

127
00:14:53,305 --> 00:14:54,785
Do you have a boyfriend now?

128
00:14:55,385 --> 00:14:56,625
What are you talking about?

129
00:15:00,745 --> 00:15:02,945
I heard your assistant
call that guy brother-in-law.

130
00:15:05,425 --> 00:15:06,705
He's not my boyfriend.

131
00:15:07,945 --> 00:15:09,025
He's my fiancé.

132
00:15:26,745 --> 00:15:27,745
Is Luke still alive?

133
00:15:28,785 --> 00:15:30,745
Luke's still young. Why wouldn't he be?

134
00:15:30,825 --> 00:15:31,865
Is he at home?

135
00:15:32,705 --> 00:15:33,545
Yeah.

136
00:15:35,145 --> 00:15:36,305
I want to see him.

137
00:15:39,545 --> 00:15:40,745
I don't want Luke to see you.

138
00:15:40,825 --> 00:15:42,105
He'd be heartbroken.

139
00:15:46,105 --> 00:15:47,305
Even Luke misses me.

140
00:15:49,105 --> 00:15:50,265
You're worse than a dog.

141
00:15:53,665 --> 00:15:54,745
Luan Nian.

142
00:15:56,505 --> 00:15:58,945
We've been tangled up for so many years.

143
00:15:59,025 --> 00:16:00,105
I'm exhausted.

144
00:16:02,105 --> 00:16:03,385
Now,

145
00:16:04,065 --> 00:16:05,945
I just want to live my own life,

146
00:16:06,625 --> 00:16:08,225
take care of my family,

147
00:16:08,305 --> 00:16:10,745
and put my life back in order.

148
00:16:12,225 --> 00:16:13,705
I don't want anything else.

149
00:16:15,145 --> 00:16:18,185
If you have to know
why I left without saying goodbye,

150
00:16:19,065 --> 00:16:23,905
it's because I knew if I'd said goodbye,
you would've said a lot of hurtful things.

151
00:16:23,985 --> 00:16:25,505
I'd had enough of that.

152
00:16:35,465 --> 00:16:36,305
Finished?

153
00:16:37,505 --> 00:16:38,425
Yeah.

154
00:16:39,825 --> 00:16:41,185
Then let me say a few things.

155
00:16:43,665 --> 00:16:44,545
Go ahead.

156
00:16:44,625 --> 00:16:47,225
There's something I think
you deserve to hear from me.

157
00:16:49,025 --> 00:16:50,465
Back when you were up
for the Specialist title,

158
00:16:51,305 --> 00:16:54,345
I gave you a very high score.

159
00:16:54,425 --> 00:16:56,905
I only found out afterward that Song Ying
had been added as your competitor.

160
00:16:58,425 --> 00:16:59,625
You always told me to be fair.

161
00:17:00,505 --> 00:17:01,345
I was.

162
00:17:02,505 --> 00:17:04,424
My score reflected how I saw you.

163
00:17:05,265 --> 00:17:07,785
If you think you weren't good enough

164
00:17:07,865 --> 00:17:09,025
when you first joined Lime,

165
00:17:09,905 --> 00:17:10,865
that you lacked confidence,

166
00:17:11,865 --> 00:17:14,184
or that I looked down
on you even when you left,

167
00:17:14,265 --> 00:17:15,785
then let me make one thing clear.

168
00:17:16,305 --> 00:17:18,464
When you first joined,
you weren't very good.

169
00:17:19,745 --> 00:17:21,145
But by the time you left,

170
00:17:22,545 --> 00:17:23,865
you were the best employee
I'd ever trained.

171
00:17:26,865 --> 00:17:28,224
It was snowing that day too.

172
00:17:29,145 --> 00:17:30,545
You walked out of my place.

173
00:17:31,945 --> 00:17:34,065
You made Luke choose between you and me.

174
00:17:37,705 --> 00:17:39,745
It felt like getting divorced.

175
00:17:41,425 --> 00:17:43,345
At least people
negotiate during a divorce.

176
00:17:43,425 --> 00:17:44,505
But you?

177
00:17:44,585 --> 00:17:46,385
You just walked away.

178
00:17:48,985 --> 00:17:51,425
Did you think you were the only one who
gave your heart over the past six years?

179
00:17:52,305 --> 00:17:53,465
What about mine?

180
00:17:55,465 --> 00:17:56,865
Didn't I try?

181
00:18:07,945 --> 00:18:08,785
Luan Nian.

182
00:18:13,025 --> 00:18:14,505
I'm really grateful

183
00:18:14,585 --> 00:18:16,585
for everything you've done
for me over those years.

184
00:18:17,505 --> 00:18:18,985
I truly appreciate it.

185
00:18:20,505 --> 00:18:24,825
I already wished you well
in the last message I sent you.

186
00:18:29,865 --> 00:18:32,185
I always hope
everything goes well for you.

187
00:18:35,305 --> 00:18:36,585
But…

188
00:18:39,545 --> 00:18:41,985
we still have a long life ahead of us.

189
00:18:44,825 --> 00:18:49,825
There are so many things worth doing
and so many people worth loving.

190
00:18:56,985 --> 00:18:58,625
Go back, Luan Nian.

191
00:19:01,425 --> 00:19:02,425
I'm not leaving.

192
00:19:03,945 --> 00:19:05,425
I want to see Luke right now.

193
00:19:07,265 --> 00:19:09,225
Luke had been with me
since the day we brought him home.

194
00:19:09,865 --> 00:19:11,025
I fed him.

195
00:19:11,105 --> 00:19:13,145
I took him hiking. I walked him.

196
00:19:13,225 --> 00:19:14,945
Why can't I see him?

197
00:19:15,025 --> 00:19:16,745
Because Luke is my dog.

198
00:19:16,825 --> 00:19:18,265
Your dog's name is Luke.

199
00:19:19,505 --> 00:19:21,505
He's named after my English name.

200
00:19:27,425 --> 00:19:29,865
I trained him too. Why can't I see him?

201
00:20:17,865 --> 00:20:18,705
Tao.

202
00:20:29,945 --> 00:20:31,385
You just want to see Luke?

203
00:20:34,905 --> 00:20:35,745
Yes.

204
00:20:39,265 --> 00:20:40,105
Okay.

205
00:21:02,345 --> 00:21:03,345
Luke!

206
00:21:04,385 --> 00:21:05,225
Luke.

207
00:21:05,785 --> 00:21:06,985
Luke.

208
00:21:11,185 --> 00:21:12,425
Let me take a look at you. There, there.

209
00:21:14,585 --> 00:21:15,625
You've gotten thinner.

210
00:21:16,385 --> 00:21:17,585
She doesn't let you eat meat, does she?

211
00:21:18,705 --> 00:21:20,025
His stomach is sensitive.

212
00:21:20,105 --> 00:21:21,625
If he eats too much, he'll throw up.

213
00:21:24,425 --> 00:21:26,025
Looks like Mr. Xing
hasn't been around much.

214
00:21:30,985 --> 00:21:32,465
You had a point.

215
00:21:35,665 --> 00:21:38,745
I shouldn't stop you from seeing Luke.

216
00:21:40,105 --> 00:21:41,505
After all, you raised him.

217
00:21:42,105 --> 00:21:45,265
If you miss him, just let me know.

218
00:21:45,945 --> 00:21:47,545
You can take him out anytime.

219
00:21:52,265 --> 00:21:53,505
I have a few more things to say.

220
00:21:56,425 --> 00:21:57,265
Go ahead.

221
00:21:59,905 --> 00:22:01,025
Don't transfer money to me anymore.

222
00:22:03,145 --> 00:22:05,945
When you do, it reminds me

223
00:22:06,905 --> 00:22:09,625
of how you used to buy me expensive bags.

224
00:22:11,025 --> 00:22:13,345
It makes me very, very uncomfortable.

225
00:22:15,705 --> 00:22:17,745
And don't use any excuses
to see my parents.

226
00:22:18,985 --> 00:22:20,185
I don't like that.

227
00:22:22,585 --> 00:22:25,105
-Alright.
-One more thing.

228
00:22:26,385 --> 00:22:27,745
Things are fine the way they are now.

229
00:22:28,545 --> 00:22:29,585
Let's leave it at that.

230
00:22:36,145 --> 00:22:37,065
Luke.

231
00:22:42,305 --> 00:22:44,345
I'm going now. I'll come see you again.

232
00:23:34,625 --> 00:23:37,025
Mr. Luan, what brings you here?

233
00:23:38,505 --> 00:23:40,545
Well, my boss stepped out.

234
00:23:41,785 --> 00:23:43,625
Please have a seat. I'll give her a call.

235
00:23:44,305 --> 00:23:45,225
No need.

236
00:23:45,305 --> 00:23:47,465
I was just passing by.
I'll leave in a minute.

237
00:23:48,785 --> 00:23:49,825
Have a seat, please.

238
00:23:51,865 --> 00:23:53,505
-Is this her desk?
-Yeah.

239
00:24:04,065 --> 00:24:05,905
SUPPLIER CONTACTS

240
00:24:08,345 --> 00:24:09,185
You like coffee.

241
00:24:09,265 --> 00:24:10,505
Iced Americano.

242
00:24:10,585 --> 00:24:12,105
One moment, please. I'll go buy one now.

243
00:24:12,185 --> 00:24:14,585
Who trained your staff
on client reception?

244
00:24:14,665 --> 00:24:15,625
My boss.

245
00:24:15,705 --> 00:24:17,185
She always says,

246
00:24:17,265 --> 00:24:20,425
"Be tactful when you work,
and never lose your principles."

247
00:24:21,025 --> 00:24:22,305
Anything but sleeping
with clients is fine.

248
00:24:25,705 --> 00:24:27,265
No sleeping with clients?
Did she really say that?

249
00:24:29,865 --> 00:24:30,745
No.

250
00:24:31,985 --> 00:24:33,705
I was trying to be funny.

251
00:24:34,785 --> 00:24:37,745
What she meant was,
be observant and know what people need.

252
00:24:42,385 --> 00:24:43,345
How long have you worked here?

253
00:24:44,185 --> 00:24:45,745
Two years.

254
00:24:48,905 --> 00:24:51,545
Does your boss go on dates often?

255
00:24:54,225 --> 00:24:56,465
Go on dates?

256
00:24:57,025 --> 00:24:58,425
Not at all.

257
00:24:59,465 --> 00:25:01,665
We usually don't get off work until ten.

258
00:25:01,745 --> 00:25:03,265
She stays even later than we do.

259
00:25:03,345 --> 00:25:04,785
So I'd say no.

260
00:25:06,745 --> 00:25:07,785
Are you sure?

261
00:25:08,745 --> 00:25:09,865
I'm sure.

262
00:25:12,985 --> 00:25:14,025
Alright.

263
00:25:15,705 --> 00:25:17,225
The restroom is outside to your right.

264
00:25:17,985 --> 00:25:19,665
I'll get going. I'll visit again sometime.

265
00:25:21,945 --> 00:25:22,825
Take care, Mr. Luan.

266
00:25:30,545 --> 00:25:31,745
Dates?

267
00:25:32,425 --> 00:25:34,265
Why was he asking about that?

268
00:25:51,265 --> 00:25:53,625
-Can I ask you something?
-What is it? You seem anxious.

269
00:25:53,705 --> 00:25:56,345
Are the advertising budgets
for your clients' regional branches

270
00:25:56,425 --> 00:25:57,385
handled separately?

271
00:25:59,425 --> 00:26:01,425
That's usually the case.

272
00:26:01,505 --> 00:26:03,465
The budget is allocated to each
regional office to manage on its own.

273
00:26:06,585 --> 00:26:08,745
A friend of mine
runs an ad agency in Harbin.

274
00:26:09,305 --> 00:26:10,785
Send some budget their way
and let them give it a shot.

275
00:26:12,465 --> 00:26:13,585
Let me put it this way.

276
00:26:14,185 --> 00:26:16,025
Every agency I've introduced to you
does honest work.

277
00:26:16,105 --> 00:26:17,425
They're all solid teams.

278
00:26:19,665 --> 00:26:21,585
Say no more. I know.

279
00:26:21,665 --> 00:26:22,745
It's Shang Zhitao, right?

280
00:26:29,865 --> 00:26:31,945
I'll give you the contact.
Get in touch with them yourself.

281
00:26:32,025 --> 00:26:32,945
The contact person is Fu Dong.

282
00:26:37,665 --> 00:26:40,505
You've been to Harbin so many times

283
00:26:41,225 --> 00:26:42,345
and still got nowhere.

284
00:26:51,785 --> 00:26:52,865
Is Shang Zhitao married?

285
00:26:54,945 --> 00:26:55,945
None of your business.

286
00:26:58,625 --> 00:26:59,825
None of my business.

287
00:27:03,545 --> 00:27:05,225
That's satisfying.
Never thought I'd live to see

288
00:27:05,305 --> 00:27:07,025
someone like you,
who never listens to anyone,

289
00:27:07,105 --> 00:27:08,065
finally brought to heel.

290
00:27:08,145 --> 00:27:09,425
Are you done?

291
00:27:10,745 --> 00:27:13,185
Look, we're all rooting for you
to win her back.

292
00:27:14,065 --> 00:27:16,665
But could you be
a little more straightforward?

293
00:27:17,825 --> 00:27:19,865
If you love someone, just say it.

294
00:27:19,945 --> 00:27:21,505
Be sweet.

295
00:27:22,265 --> 00:27:24,425
Be gentle. See her often.

296
00:27:25,225 --> 00:27:27,785
Take it one step at a time. Don't rush it.

297
00:27:44,585 --> 00:27:47,585
PASTEURIZED EGGS

298
00:27:53,905 --> 00:27:54,745
Who is it?

299
00:27:56,865 --> 00:27:57,905
Why are you here again?

300
00:27:58,505 --> 00:27:59,465
I'm here to see Luke.

301
00:28:00,185 --> 00:28:01,425
Did you tell me in advance?

302
00:28:01,505 --> 00:28:03,705
Luke. Luke.

303
00:28:06,305 --> 00:28:08,345
Look. Look what I brought.

304
00:28:08,425 --> 00:28:11,185
I bought meat.
I'll make you some meatballs later.

305
00:28:11,265 --> 00:28:12,545
You need to fatten up. Good boy.

306
00:28:19,425 --> 00:28:20,305
Let's go, Luke.

307
00:28:22,505 --> 00:28:23,465
Come on.

308
00:28:23,545 --> 00:28:24,865
Luke.

309
00:28:31,945 --> 00:28:32,945
Luke.

310
00:28:35,905 --> 00:28:36,905
Luke.

311
00:28:37,545 --> 00:28:38,945
Look at you drooling.

312
00:28:39,545 --> 00:28:40,585
I'll make them for you later.

313
00:28:43,825 --> 00:28:45,785
I ran into your neighbor
downstairs earlier today.

314
00:28:46,305 --> 00:28:47,905
She asked if I was your boyfriend.

315
00:28:51,065 --> 00:28:51,985
And?

316
00:28:53,425 --> 00:28:54,465
I said yes.

317
00:28:57,225 --> 00:28:59,705
It's fine. My reputation is bad anyway.

318
00:29:01,985 --> 00:29:03,505
That's a relief.

319
00:29:03,585 --> 00:29:05,265
Mine isn't great either.

320
00:29:05,345 --> 00:29:06,905
Two jerks. Perfect match.

321
00:29:09,545 --> 00:29:13,185
Luke, did you hear what he said?

322
00:29:13,265 --> 00:29:15,065
How about we poison him
so he can't talk anymore?

323
00:30:48,585 --> 00:30:49,425
Tao.

324
00:30:50,665 --> 00:30:51,785
Tao.

325
00:30:51,865 --> 00:30:53,105
Oh my.

326
00:30:53,185 --> 00:30:54,745
Mom. Dad.

327
00:30:55,345 --> 00:30:56,745
Why are you here?

328
00:30:56,825 --> 00:30:58,905
There weren't many customers today.

329
00:30:58,985 --> 00:31:01,745
Your dad said we'd bring you some food.

330
00:31:04,705 --> 00:31:06,385
What's wrong?

331
00:31:07,105 --> 00:31:07,945
Can't we come?

332
00:31:08,025 --> 00:31:10,065
Look at this girl. Well, well.

333
00:31:10,145 --> 00:31:11,385
-Honestly.
-Dad, Mom.

334
00:31:11,985 --> 00:31:12,785
Oh my!

335
00:31:13,385 --> 00:31:14,145
Mr. and Mrs. Shang, you are here.

336
00:31:16,225 --> 00:31:17,065
Mr. and Mrs. Shang.

337
00:31:18,185 --> 00:31:19,145
You have a guest?

338
00:31:21,785 --> 00:31:23,065
What is he doing here?

339
00:31:24,265 --> 00:31:25,345
Uh, he…

340
00:31:26,705 --> 00:31:28,025
Well.

341
00:31:28,105 --> 00:31:31,705
Luke has been sick,
so he came to take care of him.

342
00:31:32,985 --> 00:31:34,105
That's right.

343
00:31:34,185 --> 00:31:36,625
Tao is busy,
so I'm helping look after Luke.

344
00:31:41,105 --> 00:31:42,505
Are you cooking?

345
00:31:44,625 --> 00:31:45,745
Perfect timing.

346
00:31:45,825 --> 00:31:47,625
Let's stay and eat together.

347
00:31:48,265 --> 00:31:49,625
We've got guests.

348
00:31:49,705 --> 00:31:50,745
Don't just stand there.

349
00:31:50,825 --> 00:31:52,625
Lend him a hand.

350
00:31:52,705 --> 00:31:53,825
Help with what?

351
00:31:53,905 --> 00:31:55,945
I'm here to eat, not to work.

352
00:32:04,425 --> 00:32:05,905
Well. Luan…

353
00:32:06,425 --> 00:32:07,785
Luan Nian.

354
00:32:08,545 --> 00:32:09,425
Want a drink?

355
00:32:10,385 --> 00:32:11,545
Sure. I'll have a drink with you.

356
00:32:11,625 --> 00:32:12,625
Come.

357
00:32:15,265 --> 00:32:18,425
The first toast is for you.

358
00:32:18,505 --> 00:32:20,345
Welcome to Harbin.

359
00:32:20,945 --> 00:32:22,065
Thank you, Mr. Shang.

360
00:32:28,265 --> 00:32:29,105
The second toast.

361
00:32:30,305 --> 00:32:31,665
Thank you

362
00:32:31,745 --> 00:32:33,545
for supporting our tavern last time.

363
00:32:34,225 --> 00:32:35,225
My pleasure.

364
00:32:39,945 --> 00:32:41,545
Not eating the dishes?

365
00:32:41,625 --> 00:32:43,025
The third toast.

366
00:32:43,105 --> 00:32:44,145
Thank you

367
00:32:45,185 --> 00:32:47,185
and your friends for looking after her

368
00:32:47,265 --> 00:32:50,265
when Tao was all alone in Beijing.

369
00:32:51,065 --> 00:32:52,145
Come on.

370
00:32:54,585 --> 00:32:55,545
Have a bite.

371
00:32:55,625 --> 00:32:57,305
-Soak up the alcohol. Eat the dishes.
-Here.

372
00:32:57,385 --> 00:33:00,665
Also, thank you for taking care of Luke.

373
00:33:01,265 --> 00:33:03,105
Are you sure you want to continue?

374
00:33:03,865 --> 00:33:05,905
Don't worry. He's a young man.

375
00:33:05,985 --> 00:33:06,905
Well.

376
00:33:09,185 --> 00:33:10,545
That's enough.

377
00:33:10,625 --> 00:33:11,625
At least eat something.

378
00:33:20,185 --> 00:33:21,545
Here. Drink it.

379
00:33:21,625 --> 00:33:22,705
Sure.

380
00:33:24,265 --> 00:33:25,145
Thank you.

381
00:33:25,225 --> 00:33:26,505
Are you hiding something from me?

382
00:33:26,585 --> 00:33:27,465
You looked after Luke well.

383
00:33:28,345 --> 00:33:30,665
-I'm not.
-Wishing Luke good health as he grows up.

384
00:33:30,745 --> 00:33:31,905
You're hiding something from your mom.

385
00:33:31,985 --> 00:33:33,785
Don't interrupt.

386
00:33:34,785 --> 00:33:36,145
Listen to me.

387
00:33:36,825 --> 00:33:38,345
You… You…

388
00:33:39,145 --> 00:33:40,585
Have you thought this through?

389
00:33:40,665 --> 00:33:42,305
I'm always on your side.

390
00:33:43,185 --> 00:33:45,225
-I'm really not hiding anything.
-Tell me.

391
00:33:46,265 --> 00:33:48,385
-A spoiled child never turns out well.
-Come on.

392
00:33:48,465 --> 00:33:49,385
One more…

393
00:33:49,465 --> 00:33:51,265
-You're hiding something from me.
-Here you go.

394
00:33:51,345 --> 00:33:52,225
That's the last.

395
00:33:52,865 --> 00:33:54,465
-Come on.
-Don't let him drink anymore.

396
00:33:54,545 --> 00:33:55,385
-Here you go.
-Oh my.

397
00:33:55,465 --> 00:33:57,505
Luke is closer to you

398
00:33:58,265 --> 00:34:00,505
than he is to Tao. Drink up.

399
00:34:00,585 --> 00:34:01,945
Stop drinking, Dad.

400
00:34:02,025 --> 00:34:02,945
-He can drink himself.
-Shang.

401
00:34:03,025 --> 00:34:04,545
-Shang, stop it. No.
-Luan, cheers.

402
00:34:04,625 --> 00:34:05,545
-He's drunk enough.
-What now?

403
00:34:05,625 --> 00:34:07,425
-I'll finish it.
-Don't drink anymore.

404
00:34:11,225 --> 00:34:13,264
-Lan.
-Lan is not his name.

405
00:34:13,344 --> 00:34:14,264
It's Luan.

406
00:34:14,344 --> 00:34:15,585
Not Lan.

407
00:34:15,665 --> 00:34:17,105
-Luan.
-Yes, I'm Luan.

408
00:34:17,185 --> 00:34:18,665
Mr. Shang, let's keep drinking.

409
00:34:18,744 --> 00:34:20,665
-No.
-Let's drink some more.

410
00:34:20,744 --> 00:34:21,905
-Stop it. Don't.
-That's enough.

411
00:34:21,985 --> 00:34:23,545
My daughter needs to rest.

412
00:34:23,625 --> 00:34:24,705
Which hotel are you staying at?

413
00:34:24,784 --> 00:34:25,865
Not drinking anymore?

414
00:34:29,625 --> 00:34:30,505
Where's he staying?

415
00:34:30,585 --> 00:34:32,425
-How would I know?
-The room next door?

416
00:34:32,505 --> 00:34:34,185
I asked which hotel.

417
00:34:34,264 --> 00:34:36,344
I'm staying at the hotel
next door, Mrs. Shang.

418
00:34:36,425 --> 00:34:37,824
Alright. Let's go.

419
00:34:37,905 --> 00:34:38,744
We'll leave together.

420
00:34:38,824 --> 00:34:39,665
Oh my…

421
00:34:39,744 --> 00:34:41,545
-Not drinking anymore?
-Are you leaving already?

422
00:34:41,625 --> 00:34:42,705
Easy there.

423
00:34:44,545 --> 00:34:46,425
-Young man. Young man, wait.
-That's not the door.

424
00:34:46,505 --> 00:34:47,545
That's not the door.

425
00:34:47,625 --> 00:34:49,865
He's a lightweight.

426
00:34:49,945 --> 00:34:50,865
-Easy.
-I'm fine.

427
00:34:50,945 --> 00:34:51,824
I can walk by myself.

428
00:34:51,905 --> 00:34:53,264
Don't throw my dad's back out.

429
00:34:53,344 --> 00:34:55,744
-Walk by yourself. Let him walk.
-Go on.

430
00:34:55,824 --> 00:34:57,025
-Slow down.
-I'm fine.

431
00:34:57,105 --> 00:34:58,505
Easy.

432
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:00,425
Can he make it?

433
00:35:00,505 --> 00:35:02,505
-Can he make it?
-He's a young man.

434
00:35:02,585 --> 00:35:03,545
He holds his liquor well.

435
00:35:04,065 --> 00:35:05,825
He's well-mannered when he's drunk.

436
00:35:05,905 --> 00:35:07,425
You got him completely wasted.

437
00:35:07,505 --> 00:35:08,425
You poured him drink after drink.

438
00:35:08,505 --> 00:35:09,625
He didn't even have a bite to eat.

439
00:35:09,705 --> 00:35:11,305
The way someone acts
when they're drunk says a lot about them.

440
00:35:11,385 --> 00:35:13,145
At least this trip wasn't for nothing.

441
00:35:14,305 --> 00:35:16,265
Alright. Go get some rest.

442
00:35:16,345 --> 00:35:17,185
Go to bed early.

443
00:35:18,945 --> 00:35:19,905
-Luan.
-Bye.

444
00:35:19,985 --> 00:35:20,825
Wait.

445
00:35:20,905 --> 00:35:22,625
-Let's go together.
-Easy now.

446
00:35:22,705 --> 00:35:25,305
-Come.
-What's the rush?

447
00:35:52,425 --> 00:35:54,185
Why are you back?

448
00:35:55,705 --> 00:35:57,785
The hotel's fully booked. Excuse me.

449
00:36:01,585 --> 00:36:02,425
I have nowhere else to stay.

450
00:36:11,905 --> 00:36:13,305
Weren't you drunk?

451
00:36:14,865 --> 00:36:16,345
That wasn't enough to do it.

452
00:36:16,425 --> 00:36:17,385
You were faking.

453
00:36:19,465 --> 00:36:20,545
I'll take the guest room.

454
00:36:21,065 --> 00:36:22,505
Did I tell you to undress?

455
00:36:22,585 --> 00:36:24,225
Did I say yes?

456
00:36:26,945 --> 00:36:28,945
Knowing how hospitable
people in Harbin are,

457
00:36:29,025 --> 00:36:30,585
you wouldn't leave me out
on the street, would you?

458
00:36:31,425 --> 00:36:32,865
What exactly… Luan Nian.

459
00:36:35,825 --> 00:36:36,865
What do you want?

460
00:36:39,905 --> 00:36:41,105
I'll sleep on the couch if I have to.

461
00:36:49,825 --> 00:36:50,945
Suit yourself.

462
00:38:24,825 --> 00:38:25,665
Shang Zhitao,

463
00:38:27,585 --> 00:38:28,865
I know you're still awake.

464
00:38:30,025 --> 00:38:31,265
Just let me say a few things.

465
00:38:32,825 --> 00:38:33,745
You don't have to answer.

466
00:38:38,905 --> 00:38:41,345
After you left, I thought about us a lot.

467
00:38:44,025 --> 00:38:45,905
I know you put up with a lot

468
00:38:47,465 --> 00:38:49,025
in our relationship.

469
00:38:51,025 --> 00:38:54,385
You endured so much just to be with me
because you loved me.

470
00:38:58,745 --> 00:39:00,105
But back then,

471
00:39:01,145 --> 00:39:02,225
I was too arrogant.

472
00:39:03,905 --> 00:39:05,105
I realized everything too late.

473
00:39:07,145 --> 00:39:08,305
I didn't treat you well enough.

474
00:39:11,185 --> 00:39:12,785
But my feelings were real.

475
00:39:14,665 --> 00:39:15,905
I'm sure you could tell.

476
00:39:30,145 --> 00:39:32,265
When I said I wanted to take care
of Luke with you, I meant it.

477
00:39:34,105 --> 00:39:35,265
We've still got a long road ahead.

478
00:39:36,745 --> 00:39:37,785
I'll take it one step at a time.

479
00:39:44,345 --> 00:39:45,185
Shang Zhitao,

480
00:39:48,065 --> 00:39:48,905
I'm sorry.

481
00:39:51,505 --> 00:39:52,785
For everything that happened.

482
00:40:18,985 --> 00:40:20,465
The old me always thought

483
00:40:21,865 --> 00:40:23,625
I wasn't good enough.

484
00:40:24,825 --> 00:40:26,345
Even so, I knew I was loved.

485
00:40:29,545 --> 00:40:30,905
We really did love each other.

486
00:40:32,225 --> 00:40:34,145
But he was too proud,

487
00:40:34,745 --> 00:40:36,065
and I was too insecure.

488
00:40:36,705 --> 00:40:39,545
Neither of us would back down.

489
00:40:41,305 --> 00:40:42,145
Why?

490
00:40:42,945 --> 00:40:44,625
Why is he always like this?

491
00:40:45,265 --> 00:40:47,265
Every time I make up my mind,

492
00:40:49,785 --> 00:40:53,145
he shows up and undoes
everything I've worked so hard for.

493
00:41:21,185 --> 00:41:22,185
Why are you here?

494
00:41:22,265 --> 00:41:23,865
I brought Luke breakfast.

495
00:41:23,945 --> 00:41:25,985
I'll check on him
before heading to the airport.

496
00:41:30,585 --> 00:41:31,745
Luke.

497
00:41:35,585 --> 00:41:36,785
Luke.

498
00:41:36,865 --> 00:41:38,145
Come here, Luke.

499
00:41:41,345 --> 00:41:42,785
Come, let's not eat bread.

500
00:41:43,585 --> 00:41:45,305
It's not good. It has no nutrition.

501
00:42:08,705 --> 00:42:10,465
Shang Zhitao, is this how you live?

502
00:42:11,345 --> 00:42:12,745
You don't even have an egg in the fridge.

503
00:42:12,825 --> 00:42:15,585
Mr. Luan, I don't know how to cook.

504
00:42:16,545 --> 00:42:19,465
Ms. Shang, you can always
learn to cook for yourself.

505
00:42:19,545 --> 00:42:21,745
Why would I learn?

506
00:42:21,825 --> 00:42:24,785
I can order takeout or eat at my mom's.

507
00:42:24,865 --> 00:42:26,265
Worst case,

508
00:42:26,825 --> 00:42:28,545
I'll find a boyfriend who can cook.

509
00:42:31,185 --> 00:42:33,865
Don't you already have one?
Isn't he your fiancé?

510
00:42:34,745 --> 00:42:36,585
Want me to remind him
to come cook for you?

511
00:42:36,665 --> 00:42:39,545
Tell him to step up his game.

512
00:42:44,185 --> 00:42:45,025
I'll cook for you.

513
00:42:46,665 --> 00:42:47,825
And for Luke.

514
00:42:50,865 --> 00:42:51,985
I've got to get to work.

